redfin 1198: kern.sweet_mesa_match=2, TA-identified Touch ID matches delivered UNVERIFIED, with SEP-like keybag unlock

Owner decision 2026-11-18 ("let's just start enabling matching"): no keymaster HAT check in mode 2.
- SweetMesa (on 1192f): kern.sweet_mesa_match 0 no identity matches (boot default), 1 HAT-verified only,
  2 TA-identified matches unverified, each logged "UNVERIFIED match delivered: fid score user flags".
  MatchMode carrying an SMFP identity at +8 (BKOptionMatchForExtendEnrollment, Settings phase 2) is an
  extend-enrolment: matches go back with flags 0 and nothing is unlocked; sweetfpcd gets u32 flags bit 0 = extend.
  Other matches call sweet_pc_bio_unlock(): allowed -> flag 5 (Unlocked) when it unlocked + one SweetACM
  BiometryMatched credential armed (sweet_acm_note_verified_match); refused -> a no-identity record.
  8 AlignmentData / 17 RequestTopologyOfTemplate answer zeros. kern.sweet_mesa_state gains the counters.
- sweet_passcode.c (on 1195-1197): sweet_pc_bio_unlock / sweet_pc_bio_failed with iOS's rules: passcode entered
  since boot, within 48 h, fewer than 5 failed Touch ID matches since, no backoff. kern.sweet_passcode_bio (RO).

